rate observations.\",\"The selected report demonstrates absence: it tabulates exactly one rate per housing, states n = 9 housings per arm, and reports df = 14.3, which is only consistent with a 9-vs-9 per-housing test (a 72-row analysis would give roughly 70 df).\",\"Spot-checked arithmetic confirms the report reflects the per-housing analysis: H01 slope 7.64 recomputes exactly from its four inspections, and group means 7.79 vs 3.84 and difference 3.95 match the tabulated rates.\",\"No authority lock was minted, so the lock-consistency question is not applicable.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"absence","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent unit housing_id matches the frozen data: 18 housings each with exactly 4 monthly rows, coating constant within housing, 9 epoxy_control vs 9 silicone_hydrogel across both procedure arms.","The workflow reduces each housing's 4 inspections to one OLS slope and runs Welch's t-test on the 18 per-housing rates, so repeated measurements never enter the row-independent procedure as separate observations.","The selected report demonstrates absence: it tabulates exactly one rate per housing, states n = 9 housings per arm, and reports df = 14.3, which is only consistent with a 9-vs-9 per-housing test (a 72-row analysis would give roughly 70 df).","Spot-checked arithmetic confirms the report reflects the per-housing analysis: H01 slope 7.64 recomputes exactly from its four inspections, and group means 7.79 vs 3.84 and difference 3.95 match the tabulated rates.","No authority lock was minted, so the lock-consistency question is not applicable."]},"ttft_ms":7074,"ttft_stream_ms":1871,"time_to_request_ms":13,"type":"result","duration_ms":21222,"uuid":"32656918-b5bc-4916-8f1e-3c44a8d5c044"}
